WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320
OK, so we're going to pick up from where we left off the last day.

2
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.040
And I will read it and just comment as we go along.

3
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.560
Is that all right?

4
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.400
The way I do this is that if I read it slowly and meaningfully

5
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.000
and prayerfully, the Lord illuminates me and I illuminate you.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.600
It's a good method.

7
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.280
And as matter how much I prepare it,

8
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.600
I still get something when I'm reading it.

9
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.440
It's really amazing.

10
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.000
So, for example, Louisa said, if I woke up in the morning,

11
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.280
now she's talking about a time when the Lord is teaching her

12
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:37.200
a lot of mortification and self-discipline.

13
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.840
If I didn't get up immediately, she said,

14
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:45.120
the interior voice would tell me, you rest and I had no other bed but the cross.

15
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.680
Now, I know you don't use the snooze button or anything, you know?

16
00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:50.840
And when your alarm clock goes off.

17
00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.840
But what the Lord was asking her is as soon as she woke up

18
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.040
that she was to have the discipline of actually getting out of bed,

19
00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.400
that's very difficult, unless it's the end of the world or something.

20
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.000
I would find that difficult, I don't know about you.

21
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.000
So, if I walked and my sight would run a little further,

22
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.560
he would immediately reprimand me, I don't want this.

23
00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.840
You're to let your sight,

24
00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.120
you're not to let your sight move away

25
00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:20.200
but the length of your step so that you won't trip.

26
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:24.480
If I was in the countryside and I saw flowers and trees he would say to me,

27
00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.840
"I've created everything for love of you and you,

28
00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.960
deprive your sight of this pleasure for love of me."

29
00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.760
Even the most innocent and holy things,

30
00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.880
as for example, the cloths for the altars, the processions,

31
00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.080
he would say to me,

32
00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:45.120
"You must take no pleasure but in me alone."

33
00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.800
If I was sitting while working he would say to me,

34
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.200
"You're too comfortable.

35
00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.520
Don't you remember that my life was a continuous suffering and you, you?"

36
00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.440
In order to content him, I would immediately shift,

37
00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:00.400
"Watch the sense of humor coming out to half the chair,

38
00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:04.400
leaving the other half empty and sometimes jokingly I'd say to him,

39
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.880
"See Lord, the other halves for you."

40
00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.560
Common sit near me.

41
00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:12.480
I'll give you a comment when I just read this section.

42
00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.760
Sometimes it seemed that he would content me

43
00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:19.960
and I felt such delight that I myself cannot express it.

44
00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:23.160
Sometimes then, when I was working a little slowly

45
00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:27.960
and listlessly, her work was mostly crochet, needlework,

46
00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.880
that kind of stuff.

47
00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:33.320
He would say to me, "Hurry up, hurry up, hurry yourself.

48
00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.880
For the time you gain by helping yourself,

49
00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.160
you will spend with me in prayer."

50
00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.520
Sometimes he himself would assign to me

51
00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.320
how much work I was supposed to do

52
00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.520
and then I would pray him to come and help me.

53
00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:49.040
Yes, yes, he would say, "We will do it together."

54
00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.200
This is the first "we" in the whole thing.

55
00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.760
Up to now, he says this and I respond.

56
00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.920
This is the "we", the shift from "I" to "we".

57
00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.640
We will do it together so that when you have finished,

58
00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.800
we will be more free.

59
00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:09.040
Now, notice the claim on union that's actually there.

60
00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.640
And it would happen that in one hour or two,

61
00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.320
I did what I was supposed to do for the whole day

62
00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.040
and then I would go to pray and he gave me such light

63
00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:21.840
which is enlightenment or understanding

64
00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.320
and told me many things,

65
00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:25.640
such that it would be too long for me to say them all.

66
00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:29.560
Now, why is he telling her she has to live such a restricted life?

67
00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.600
You're not to smell the flowers.

68
00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.800
You're not to look down the street to see what,

69
00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:36.320
you're going to look one step ahead.

70
00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.400
What is he preparing her for?

71
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.360
He's preparing her for the fact that she will have to make

72
00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:47.440
an unbelievable sacrifice of sitting in a bed for 64 years.

73
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.920
At this moment, she doesn't know that's what's being asked of her.

74
00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:56.840
All she knows is that the parameters of her life are dwindling

75
00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.840
and she's being brought down to a much smaller space

76
00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:03.160
to get used to a much smaller space

77
00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:07.320
so that he can work with her.

78
00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.480
And she accepts this discipline.

79
00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:13.360
Now, is he asking the same thing of you?

80
00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:16.360
The answer is no, you're not called

81
00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.920
to the sacrifice that was asked of her.

82
00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:21.560
So, what you apply to yourself in this

83
00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:25.720
is the discipline of generosity in everyday life

84
00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:28.600
that you're not indulging yourself in everything you do.

85
00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:32.480
Just the ordinary discipline is actually required of us.

86
00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:37.280
So, the next paragraph, the heading I put on it is the Lord provides.

87
00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:40.560
Yahweh Jairah, the Lord provides.

88
00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.640
I remember that while I was alone working,

89
00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:47.120
I noticed that the thread was not enough to finish that work

90
00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:51.080
and that I would need to go to my family in order to get some more.

91
00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:55.400
So, I said to him, "What's the purpose of having helped me, my beloved?

92
00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.560
"As I see that I need to go to my family,

93
00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:01.280
"I may find people who may prevent me from coming back here,

94
00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:04.360
"and this time, our conversation will come to nothing."

95
00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.960
"What? What?" he said to me, "Don't you have faith?"

96
00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:11.080
"Yes," Louisa said, "Well, then, have no fear

97
00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.320
"for I will make you complete everything,

98
00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:17.840
"and so what happened, the thread just kept going."

99
00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:21.840
So, she's learning to depend on him absolutely.

100
00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.400
Now, the thing is the Lord will do it for you as well

101
00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.120
if you come up with the same trust.

102
00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:31.920
I had an eye-opening experience in Soweto in South Africa,

103
00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:34.840
which had a very bad name because of the media,

104
00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:38.320
giving you the impression that everybody in Soweto was a baddie.

105
00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.600
There's only three million people in Soweto.

106
00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:41.800
They're not all baddies.

107
00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.400
I absolutely loved being there.

108
00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.440
And the parish that I was in,

109
00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:49.640
there was 24-hours adoration, the church never closed,

110
00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:53.320
and there was never more than 20 or 25 people in adoration.

111
00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:56.080
Morning noon and night was absolutely incredible.

112
00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.520
The priest told me he was so happy

113
00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:00.280
he was praying that the bishop would forget he was there.

114
00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:01.800
(audience laughing)

115
00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:04.640
But their Mass on a Sunday went on for three hours.

116
00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.480
So, I attended two of these Masses

117
00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:09.160
and had six hours of liturgy for the morning

118
00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.080
'cause I was speaking at the Masses.

119
00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:13.680
And at the end of the second one, the priest said to me,

120
00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.080
"We're inviting you for a special experience."

121
00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.440
I said, "Well, that's fine."

122
00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.680
He said, "Come and have lunch."

123
00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.320
I thought, "What's so special about lunch?"

124
00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:22.680
You know what I mean?

125
00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:26.080
But what was so special about lunch was that at the offer tree,

126
00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:29.120
they brought in the chickens with the legs tied

127
00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:30.640
and they brought in the vegetables

128
00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:31.760
and they brought in the fruits

129
00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.440
and they brought in everything.

130
00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:36.520
And lunch was whatever was offered at the offer tree.

131
00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:42.720
So, when we went out, there were the ladies cooking

132
00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:44.600
what was actually offered

133
00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:46.960
and the double doors were opened

134
00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:50.360
and there was a huge sign out towards the street

135
00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:53.400
and it said, "If you were not able to join us

136
00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:57.120
"for the Eucharist, please join us for our agape meal."

137
00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:02.280
So, the invitation was opened to absolutely anybody.

138
00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:05.840
And I sat in that room from about one o'clock

139
00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:10.880
until about four and counted approximately 350 people

140
00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.360
coming for the meal.

141
00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:15.040
And the meal didn't finish

142
00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:18.720
and the last person offered their plate for food.

143
00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:20.720
And I said to the priest,

144
00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:23.640
you did not get enough food at that altar

145
00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:25.920
'cause I was there for 350 people.

146
00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.520
No, he said, he definitely didn't.

147
00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:30.720
He said, "We have the multiplication of the loaves

148
00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:35.120
"every single Sunday for the past 25 years."

149
00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:39.280
He said, "We don't ask God for it.

150
00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:43.360
"We just trust the people, we'll bring the food."

151
00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:44.960
And he said, "There's never enough.

152
00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:50.000
"There was enough food for about 50 people offered today at Mass."

153
00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.520
And he said, "It just kept multiplying."

154
00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:52.960
He said, "They all say,

155
00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:55.280
"Father, we're not going to eat until you're blessed."

156
00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:56.600
(audience laughs)

157
00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:58.680
"We need your blessing to multiply this

158
00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:00.240
"and they have it all the time."

159
00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:03.800
And what I saw was people who had such a deep,

160
00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:08.080
simple trust in God that God delighted in doing that.

161
00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:09.640
And we're so sophisticated to see

162
00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.520
we wouldn't even think about it.

163
00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.600
You know, that's the sadness on our part.

164
00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.400
Now, Louisa is being taught

165
00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:20.400
to have this very basic, simple trust in God.

166
00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:22.520
It's really wonderful.

167
00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:25.440
And so she learns on a very simple thing

168
00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.480
that your thread will multiply,

169
00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.680
but she's going to learn it on much higher things later on.

170
00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:34.080
So in the next paragraph,

171
00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:37.680
Louisa is being prepared to be a victim's soul.

172
00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:41.520
So the next lesson is total self-abnegation.

173
00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.920
You know, total self-abnegation is total self to man.

174
00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.480
Total, total, total, you're not looking

175
00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:48.000
for anything for yourself.

176
00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:52.200
If then at lunchtime I ate something tasty,

177
00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:55.240
he would immediately reprimand me interiorly saying,

178
00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:58.080
"Have you perhaps forgotten that I had no other taste

179
00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:00.240
"but suffering for love of you?

180
00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:01.920
"And that you must have no other taste

181
00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:04.600
"but mortifying yourself for love of me."

182
00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.600
Now, Louisa isn't the only one that went down that road.

183
00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.120
I mean, St. Therese did and most of the saints

184
00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:11.720
that I've read about.

185
00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:15.640
"Leave a society," said, "and eat that which you like the least."

186
00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:17.240
Is that the way you eat your lunch?

187
00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:21.840
And I would immediately take it and bring it to the maid.

188
00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:26.000
You can see that she's in an upper-middle-class family.

189
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.920
I never lived with maids, did you?

190
00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:31.920
And I would say that I didn't want it anymore.

191
00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:36.000
And many times I remained almost on an empty stomach.

192
00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:39.480
However, when I would go to pray,

193
00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:44.000
I would receive so much strength and feel so satiated

194
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.480
that I would feel nausea for everything.

195
00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.040
Now, what she's being taught is

196
00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:53.440
you withdraw yourself from this natural food

197
00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.080
and I will feed you on supernatural food.

198
00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:58.560
This is the call to being a victim soul

199
00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:01.200
where she will be feeding mostly on the eucharist

200
00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.240
for most of her life.

201
00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:06.360
It's not what you and I are called to us.

202
00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:09.200
Other times then, in order to contradict me,

203
00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.400
if I did not feel like eating, he would say to me,

204
00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:14.600
"I want you to eat for love of me."

205
00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:16.040
This is simply self-denial.

206
00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:20.560
It's also human will surrendering to the divine will.

207
00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:23.760
And as the food unites with the body pray,

208
00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:26.480
"My love may unite with your soul."

209
00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.400
Everything will be sanctified.

210
00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:32.200
Now, is it the presence of the food

211
00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:34.840
or the absence of the food is the more holy?

212
00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:38.320
The answer is neither.

213
00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:44.120
What makes the presence or the absence of food holy

214
00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.440
is that you're surrendering to God's will.

215
00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:49.080
That's the issue and that's what she's learning.

216
00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:52.520
And later on, when she gets into taking on

217
00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:55.080
the sufferings of Christ in reparation

218
00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.560
for the church and the world, she has to learn

219
00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.080
it's not the sufferings.

220
00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:02.680
It's whether God wants it or God doesn't want it.

221
00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.120
It's God's will is the issue.

222
00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:07.160
She's going to learn that the whole way through.

223
00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:10.520
So, in a word, without going any further,

224
00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:15.520
even in the smallest things, he tried to make my will die.

225
00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.240
There is the issue.

226
00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:19.600
Now, your will doesn't die.

227
00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:23.680
But you try to push aside to let the divine will take over.

228
00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:28.120
So, for that, I want to give you the New Testament,

229
00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:29.800
full of die to self.

230
00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:32.240
One Corinthians 15, 31,

231
00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:36.840
one Corinthians 15, 31,

232
00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:41.840
and Philippians 1, 21, Philippians 1, 21.

233
00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:43.880
We must die to self.

234
00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:48.800
So, he tried to make my will die

235
00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:52.240
so that it might live only for him.

236
00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:55.920
So, that means the human will gives way

237
00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:57.960
to let the divine will take over.

238
00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:01.280
You have to have a will, otherwise you can't live.

239
00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:03.880
But if the human will is completely dominant,

240
00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:06.840
then the divine will cannot take over

241
00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:08.680
and bring you to that divine level.

242
00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:11.600
When we try to surrender to the divine will,

243
00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:15.200
then he can raise us up to the level of the divine will.

244
00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:19.880
He allowed that I be contradicted also by the confessor.

245
00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:23.360
Now, the contradiction thing is merely not my will,

246
00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:25.080
but thine be done.

247
00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:29.080
And at the early stages of walking in the divine will,

248
00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:31.760
it's terribly important to take that as a motto,

249
00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:33.720
not my will, but thine be done.

250
00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:36.200
And the Lord will allow people to cross you.

251
00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:40.280
Sometimes, totally, irrationally and everything.

252
